{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>And the firstborn bore a son and called his name Moav.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: do not read מואב but מאב (from the father) — she was not modest and publicly declared that he was born from her father. But the younger one called him by a euphemism, בן עמי. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted in Horayot (10b): the Holy One, blessed be He, does not withhold the reward for seemly speech. For the firstborn, who called him מואב, the Merciful One said to Moses (Deuteronomy 2:9): ״אל תצר את מואב ואל תתגר בם מלחמה״ — do not harass Moav and do not provoke them to battle; battle it is not, but you may distress them slightly. While the younger one, who called him בן עמי, the Merciful One said to Moses: ״אל תצורם ואל תתגר בם״ — do not besiege them and do not provoke them — altogether, even distress."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:13:46.182823618Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}